---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_supplied: investor invokes claimTokenAllocation(legionSignature, projectSignature, amount, vestingSchedule)
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert_supply: tokens not yet supplied
    q_revert_supply --> [*]: revert TokensNotSupplied
    q_check_supplied --> q_verify_legion: tokens supplied
    q_verify_legion --> q_revert_legion: Legion signature invalid
    q_revert_legion --> [*]: revert InvalidLegionSignature
    q_verify_legion --> q_verify_project: Legion signature valid
    q_verify_project --> q_revert_project: project signature invalid
    q_revert_project --> [*]: revert InvalidProjectSignature
    q_verify_project --> q_check_claimed: both signatures valid
    q_check_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: position already claimed
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_check_claimed --> q_check_vesting: not yet claimed
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vestingSchedule has time-locked portions
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: no vesting required
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_vesting: deploy vesting contract
    q_transfer_vesting --> q_mark: transfer time-locked tokens to vesting contract
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark: transfer tokens directly to investor
    q_mark --> [*]: position.claimed = true; emit TokensClaimed(investor, amount)

    note right of q_verify_legion
        INV-001: Dual-signature verification required (Legion + project)
        INV-002: Both signatures must be valid for claim to proceed
        INV-003: No Merkle proof used; dual signatures replace Merkle verification
    end note
